{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## PLAN AMENDED AND RE-CERTIFIED — ready to implement, but SERIALIZED behind 88d9\n\nThe corrected arbitration rule is now in the description and the plan review PASSES with **0 blocking\nfindings**, signed. File impact widened to four paths, adding `outbound_links.py` — suppressing only the\ninbound side would leave the pass divergent and churning.\n\nAlso fixed a stale contradiction the edit introduced, caught by grepping the whole document afterwards\n(the habit HANDOFF #4 lesson 4 prescribes): the \"G3's blind spot\" section still asserted *\"G4 closes that\nin a healthy pass, because outbound emits a link ADD for exactly that dep and the suppression drops the\nremoval\"* — which is the exact error being corrected. It now explains that precedence handles the blind\nspot instead, and the wrong sentence is quoted verbatim in the plan so the mistake stays legible rather\nthan being quietly overwritten. The residual window narrows to `seed_managed_refs_from_current` marking a\nPRE-FEATURE ticket's current deps as managed.\n\n**DO NOT START THE IMPLEMENTATION UNTIL CHANGE 1288 (88d9) LANDS.** Both modify `inbound_differ.py`, which\nsits at 773/800 after 88d9's extraction. Running them in parallel would conflict in exactly the way the\n2b16/88d9 serialization was set up to avoid.\n\nNote for whoever implements it: `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_link_removal_2b16.py`\nalready contains `test_g4_outbound_add_this_pass_suppresses_the_removal`, which asserts the WRONG\nbehaviour. **It must be rewritten, not extended** — its greenness is the reason the first version shipped\nbroken, and leaving it would pin the defect."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785768676945820001,"uuid":"9563a72f-d1e3-4622-8133-bf2b52178536"}